    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="1130" n="1118" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg1118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/11–945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-09T20:00:00-05:00">November 9, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2317. Later information from ComGen USAFIK re Dept tel 2304 Nov 7 indicates that
                    Russian officers and 100 Russian soldiers appeared at Yalu River Plant Nov 6 and
                    issued orders to remove starting Nov 8 two transformers and two generators, each
                    100,000 KVA,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d817-f1"/> and two water turbines. Normally
                    50 percent of power produced by this plant used in Korea and 50 in Manchuria.
                    August 1945 consumption figures indicate plant furnished 30 percent of power
                    used in present American zone.</p>
                <p>Full plant capacity unused since Japanese surrender due to shut down of industry
                    and two units slated for removal are therefore in stand-by status but their
                    removal would have extremely serious future consequences.</p>
                <p>In view of important bearing of this matter on commitments of both US and USSR in
                    connection with future Korean development you should, if you have not already
                    done so, make immediate and strong representations in the premises.</p>
                <pb facs="1131" n="1119" xml:id="pg1119"/>
                <p>Above information being transmitted to American Embassy, Chungking<anchor n="26"
                        xml:id="d817-f2"/> for informal and confidential transmittal to Chinese
                    Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
